ments generally safer for you and  you get lots of loot from the supply  rooms those events should get you  through the early 20s if you go between  them and main missions now here's what  you should be doing from about mid 20 to  30 hold on to a number of side missions  until you get to about your mid 20s you  can complete some of them if you need  them to get to main missions but keeping  them in reserve can help you in a number  of ways first off they scale to your  level and you could possibly get to your  high 20s and not have enough events to  do to get you over the hump the level  cap so don't complete all of the side  missions hang on to a bunch of them that  you can then complete at your level to  get to 30 now this game can be pretty  brutal if you're doing it solo because  your health doesn't naturally  generate until you're done with an  encounter so if you get in trouble call  for help from other agents or respond to  those calls for help from other agents  this is also a great thing to hold on to  if you're in your high 20s and you've  run out of activities to get to level  cap you're helping other people out  generally the game scales to your level  regardless of who you're helping so you  might be helping a really low level  player out and you also get xp for  missions that you've already done which  might be a little boring to just run  solo now if you call on those agents for  help another thing that you can do is a  hard daily bounty which unlocks at a  certain point from the White House  do not do hard bounties alone because  you have a time limit and they vanish  when you die they're also a little bit  cheap sometimes and can kill you very  quickly so I highly recommend doing them  with other people if you don't have  friends match make into it or wait for  another player to come now these final  two will give you a little bit of extra  XP one of them is go ahead and join a  clan you can just search through the  menus and find one you get XP through  group challenges and the other one is if  you really need it go pick up six weekly  Ubisoft Club challenges you can find  those off the main menu and they'll give  you just a little bit more XP each week  so that should get you to level cap if  you have tips that we haven't covered I  know we didn't talk about the dark zone  or PvP let us know in the comments below  we'd love to hear your thoughts on  getting the level cap quickly and most  importantly you don't have to get to  level cap quickly this is a big game and  if you want to take your time and enjoy  it you totally should alright thanks for  watching
 

